<Base
  title="Einbürgerungstest: Leben in DE · privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for Einbürgerungstest: Leben in DE. The app collects nothing."
>
  <PageHead title="privacy" intro="Einbürgerungstest: Leben in DE collects nothing." />
  <div class="measure doc">
    <p>The app has no accounts, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. Nothing you do in it is sent to us or to anyone else.</p>
    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your language and federal state.</li>
      <li>Which questions you have answered and how, and your mock test results.</li>
      <li>Your read-aloud speed and translation settings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These live only in the app's own storage on your device. Deleting the app deletes them.</p>
    <h2>Translating a word</h2>
    <p>When you tap a German word, the app opens Apple's system translation. Apple may process that word on its servers unless you turn on offline translation in your device settings. Apple's privacy policy applies to that step. The app itself makes no network requests.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Because the app collects no personal information, it collects none from children either.</p>
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>If this ever changes, this page will be updated before the app does. Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@mail.littleunknown.com">hello@mail.littleunknown.com</a>.</p>
    <p class="comment">Last updated 23 October 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .doc { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .doc h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
</style>
